      "url": "https://cyolo.io/company",
      "description": "About Cyolo | Simplify Secure Remote Access for OT/ICS | Cyolo New research challenges assumptions about security & productivity - Read the report Platform Cyolo PRO (Privileged Remote Operations) Cyolo CPS Segmentation Solutions By Challenge Remote Privileged Access for OT/ICS Secure Third-Party Access IT/OT Alignment Regulatory Compliance By Industry Manufacturing Energy & Utilities AI Data Centers All Industries Partners Partner Program Partner Ecosystem Technology Integrations Become a Partner Resources Resources See All Resources Events & Happy Hours News Press Releases Third Party Reports Case Studies At a Glances Datasheet White Papers Videos Featured content Press Release With Launch of CPS Segmentation, Cyolo Offers First Secure Connectivity Platform for Critical Infrastructure Case Study How Viridor Gained Visibility, Control, and Speed Across a Distributed OT Environment Blog What the Minnesota Water Attacks Reveal About Securing Remote Access to Critical Infrastructure White Paper The Paradox of Third-Party OT Access: The Surprising Benefits of Trusting Vendors Less Blog Company About Us Careers Support Toggle Search Eng De Spa Fre Ita Eng De Spa Fre Ita Get a Demo Close Menu Platform Cyolo PRO (Privileged Remote Operations) Cyolo CPS Segmentation Solutions Remote Privileged Access for OT/ICS Third-Party Secure Access IT/OT Alignment Regulatory Compliance Manufacturing Energy & Utilities Data Centers All Industries Partners Partner Program Partner Ecosystem Technology Integrations Become a Partner Resources News Press Releases Events & Happy Hours Third-Party Reports Case Studies At a Glances Datasheets White Papers Videos Blog Company About Us Careers Support Search Toggle Search Unusually Easy Secure Connectivity for Industrial Operations At Cyolo, we make it surprisingly simple to secure every connection across critical infrastructure. Manufacturing plants, data centers, and energy & utility facilities rely on Cyolo to protect both human-to-machine and machine-to-machine communications without disrupting operations. Our Mission Enable secure connectivity that drives your business instead of draining your energy Almog Apirion, our CEO and co-founder, calls himself a ‘recovering CISO.’ In that role, he saw first-hand how difficult it is to wrestle with tools that make remote connectivity complicated, slow, and inconvenient – all in the name of keeping the company secure. This was frustrating, especially because most of the tools he came across didn’t even meet his security standards. So, instead of settling for what existing solutions could do, Almog set out to create something that did what he wanted them to do: Improve operational agility for admins, supervisors, and operators. Enhance productivity for all users. Keep every session secure from start to finish. Then he assembled a team of experts and visionaries to turn that wishlist into a reality. And together, they built Cyolo. The Cyolo team started by asking some tough questions. Does security have to be so cumbersome? Or have we just learned to expect nothing better? Sure, workarounds, multiple logins, and clunky tech stacks are normal — but should they be? Should your vendor force you to migrate to the cloud or make other major infrastructure changes? You’ve spent years designing your security stack. You have better things to do than rebuild it just to meet a vendor’s needs. Shouldn’t your remote access solution work with your existing infrastructure, instead of forcing you to rip it all out and start from scratch? Different users and devices pose different levels of risk. So, why do we treat them all the same? Privileged accounts typically make up around 10% of users but are responsible for the vast majority of risk. So why not focus on them, instead of wasting resources applying rigid restrictions to everyone? Does your security vendor really need access to all your secrets? Handing over your passwords and encryption keys to a vendor only creates another weak link in your security. Shouldn’t your secrets stay secret from everyone – including your vendor? The world is decentralized. Why aren’t our access solutions? Your OT systems and operations are distributed across an increasingly wide area. Doesn't it make sense to use a remote access solution that’s similarly decentralized? It's the best way to increase uptime, improve performance, and remove the risk of a single point of compromise. Facing a difficult challenge helped us build a solution that's easy to use — and better in every way. Our leadership team keeps us on the path to perfection. Almog Apirion CEO, Co-founder Linkedin Link Dedi Yarkoni CTO, Co-founder Linkedin Link Eran Shmuely Chief Architect, Co-founder Linkedin Link Joe O’Donnell Chief Strategy Officer (CSO) Linkedin Link Gal Gonen Chief Financial Officer (CFO) Linkedin Link Asa Kedar Chief Customer Officer (CCO) Linkedin Link Mark Edge VP of Global Sales Linkedin Link Michelle Levy VP of Marketing Linkedin Link Jonathan Yellin VP of R&D Linkedin Link Michael Langer VP of Product Linkedin Link Max Berman VP of Customer Success Linkedin Link Tali Goren VP of Human Resources Linkedin Link Ian Cuthbertson VP of Global System Engineering Linkedin Link Our customers experience the Cyolo difference every day. Rapac Energy, a leading power plant operator, needed to provide secure access to their OT and SCADA systems for external suppliers, global support teams, and customers. The company previously used a VPN, but access was slow and employees were frustrated. The new solution had to include multiple security features that comply with stringent regulatory requirements and internal policies. Now, with Cyolo, Rapac is succeeding to ensure business continuity while also achieving the highest level of security for its critical systems. “No solution gives me so much control and security like Cyolo. It’s everything I need in one solution.” - Shlomo Kamilyan, CIO, Rapac Energy Read the full 