ollect or receive from or about you including on our website https://cyolo.io/ and/or the provision of our products and services. Who is Responsible for the Processing of Your Personal Information? The entity responsible for the processing of your personal information is Cyolo Security Ltd., referred to as “Cyolo”, “our”, “we” or “us” in this privacy policy. Personal information means any information that may be used to directly or indirectly identify an individual, including, but not limited to, a first and last name, email address, a home, postal or other physical address, other contact information, title, birth date, gender, occupation, industry, personal interests, and any other category of information deemed as personally identifiable information by applicable privacy laws and regulations. Information for Providing you with a Demo We collect and store your full name, company email address, telephone number, job title, company name and details and any other personal information you provide us with when requesting a demo. We use this information to establish a customer relationship and to provide you or your clients with a demo of our products. We rely on the performance of a contract or steps taken at your request before entering into a contract and/or our legitimate interest (e.g., responding to you regarding the demo request). If you do not provide this information, we will not be able to process your request for a demo. Information for Inquiries We collect and store your full name, job title, company name and details, company email address, country, inquiry type, telephone number, and any other personal information you provide us with, when you contact us through our website. We will use such information to contact you, to respond to your query and to establish a business relationship. We rely on our legitimate interest (for example, responding to your questions or establishing a business relationship). If you do not provide this information, we will not be able to establish business communications with you and/or respond to you. Information for Marketing and Promotional Purposes We collect and store your email address, if you subscribe to our newsletter, for the purpose of sending you information on promotional or informational materials, direct mailing and targeted advertising on products that we believe you may be interested in. We do so only if you have given consent for such purposes. If you do not provide us with this information, we will not be able to send you marketing communication. Information for Candidates Applying for an Open Position with Cyolo through our Website We collect your full name, email address, phone number and resume/CV, as well as additional personal information collected during the recruitment process, including interview notes, internal evaluations, and information obtained from reference checks, and any other personal information you choose to provide us. We use this information to assess you as a candidate, manage the recruitment process, communicate with you, conduct interviews and reference checks, and evaluate your suitability for current or future roles. We rely on the performance of a contract or steps taken at your request before entering into a contract and/or our legitimate interest (e.g., assessing your candidacy). If you do not provide this information, we will not be able to assess you as a candidate and/or communicate with you. Information for the Maintenance and Improvement of our Website and Services Third-party tools integrated into our website may collect and process information such as IP addresses, web server logs, cookies, pixel tags and web beacons as set forth in our Cookie Policy. You can always change your cookie preferences using your web browser settings or by changing your preferences in the cookie consent mechanism available on the website. For more information, please see our Cookie Policy. Information for Signing up to and Using our Services We collect and process your full name, e",
